Q: How to get the result from select query using Spring boot A: <p>Your service method fails because Hibernate tries to map the native SQL result to the <code>MatchCount</code> entity, but your SQL query <strong>does not return all the fields required by the entity</strong> (especially <code>id</code> and <code>user_id</code>).</p>
<p>Since the entity expects columns that are <strong>not present in your SELECT query</strong>, Hibernate throws:</p>
<pre><code>Column 'id' not found
</code></pre>
<p>The controller method works because it returns <code>List&lt;Map&lt;String,Object&gt;&gt;</code>, which does <strong>not</strong> require entity mapping. The service method fails because it tries to map the result to a <strong>JPA entity that doesn't match the SQL output</strong>.</p>
<p>Create a DTO for your SELECT result like below.</p>
<pre><code>public interface MatchRecommendationDTO {
    int getUnique_id();
    String getDate();
    String getMatch_started();
    String getTeam1();
    String getTeam2();
    int getWeight();
}
</code></pre>
<p>modify your repo like below.</p>
<pre><code>@Query(value = &quot;SELECT unique_id, date, 
                  CASE WHEN match_started = 1 THEN 'Yes' ELSE 'No' END AS match_started,
                  team1, team2, COUNT(unique_id) AS weight 
                FROM cricket_match 
                GROUP BY unique_id, date, match_started, team1, team2 
                ORDER BY COUNT(unique_id) DESC&quot;,
       nativeQuery = true)
List&lt;MatchRecommendationDTO&gt; findRecommendationDTO();
</code></pre>
<p>Then match your service and controler like given below and give a try<br />
Service changes</p>
<pre><code>public List&lt;MatchRecommendationDTO&gt; findByRecommendationServiceCall() {
    return matchCountRepository.findRecommendationDTO();
}
</code></pre>
<p>Controller changes</p>
<pre><code>@GetMapping(&quot;/matchrecommendationnew&quot;)
public List&lt;MatchRecommendationDTO&gt; getMyMatchRecommendation() {
    return matchRecommendationService.findByRecommendationServiceCall();
}
</code></pre>

Q: bootstrap modal pop up on dropdown select A: <p>You can try this....</p>

<pre><code>&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;
